    "safety": {
      "cautions": [
        "Stop if you feel sharp, radiating or nerve-type pain.",
        "Muscle glow colours and activation curves are illustrative, not measured EMG.",
        "Choose a dumbbell load you can control for every rep; the load is user-chosen.",
        "Shoulder pain, instability or limited overhead mobility: do not hold a weight overhead; practise the hinge with no load or a low windmill.",
        "Low-back pain: keep the range small; the hinge and side-bend combine under load.",
        "Never let the dumbbell drift over the head; if the arm wavers, bring the weight down and end the set."
      ],
      "modify": [
        "No weight (bodyweight windmill) or the free hand on a box to shorten the range.",
        "Dumbbell held low in the free hand instead (low windmill)."
      ],
      "regressions": [
        "Bodyweight windmill.",
        "Overhead hold or carry (no hinge)."
      ],
      "progressions": [
        "Heavier dumbbell.",
        "Kettlebell windmill (bottoms-up for advanced lifters).",
        "Turkish get-up."
      ]
    },
    "muscleNotes": {
      "obliques_r": "The obliques on the dumbbell side lower the trunk into the side-bend under control and pull it back up; side-lying lateral flexion work drove external oblique to about 98% MVC in Konrad 2001. No EMG study of the windmill was found (clinical opinion for the windmill itself).",
      "spinal_extensors_r": "Quadratus lumborum and the erector spinae on the dumbbell side hold the trunk as it hinges and bends; quadratus lumborum is a primary lateral stabiliser (McGill, Juker and Kropf).",
      "glute_max_r": "Both glutes control the hip hinge and drive the stand-up, the right hip pushed back and out (clinical opinion).",
      "glute_max_l": "Both glutes control the hip hinge and drive the stand-up, the right hip pushed back and out (clinical opinion).",
      "obliques_l": "The obliques on the free-hand side turn the chest open toward the dumbbell (clinical opinion).",
      "glute_med_r": "Steadies the pelvis over the planted feet as the hips shift (clinical opinion).",
      "glute_med_l": "Steadies the pelvis over the planted feet as the hips shift (clinical opinion).",
      "hamstrings_r": "Lengthen as the hips hinge over the nearly straight right leg (clinical opinion).",
      "hamstrings_l": "Lengthen as the hips hinge over the nearly straight right leg (clinical opinion).",
      "core": "Rectus abdominis and the deep abdominals keep the trunk braced (clinical opinion).",
      "lat_deltoid_r": "Holds the arm locked vertical overhead (clinical opinion).",
      "ant_deltoid_r": "Holds the arm locked vertical overhead (clinical opinion).",
      "serratus_r": "Keeps the shoulder blade rotated up under the load (clinical opinion).",
      "infraspinatus_r": "Rotator cuff centres the shoulder as the trunk turns under the fixed arm (clinical opinion).",
      "triceps_r": "Keeps the elbow locked (clinical opinion).",
      "upper_traps_r": "Supports the shoulder girdle under the overhead load (clinical opinion).",
      "forearm_flexors_r": "Grip the dumbbell (clinical opinion)."
    }
  },
